{"chunk_id": "2de7158353eb", "text": "Dhritarashtra laments to Sanjaya the fall of Bhishma, the Kuru grandsire, unable to comprehend how the nearly invincible warrior\u2014once undefeated even by Parashurama\u2014could be slain by Shikhandin with Arjuna\u2019s aid. Sanjaya recounts the aftermath: Bhishma lies on a bed of arrows, his body suspended above the earth, and both armies are struck with grief and awe. The natural world itself seems to mourn. Fighting halts as Kurus and Pandavas alike gather around the fallen elder. When Bhishma asks for a fitting pillow, Arjuna reverently shoots three arrows into the ground to support his head. Pleased, Bhishma praises him and declares he will remain alive on the arrow-bed until the sun turns northward (Uttarayana), demonstrating his mastery over death and embodying the warrior ideal.\nAfter Bhishma falls, warriors gather; Arjuna creates an arrow-pillow for him, and Bhishma resolves to lie on his bed of arrows until the sun\u2019s northern course.\nThemes: heroic death, warrior duty, reverence for elders, fate and timing of death", "vector": [0.0033500539138913155, -0.008518945425748825, 0.0009169005788862705, 0.00897781178355217, 0.0006496444111689925, 0.02362162061035633, -0.023701423779129982, -0.0041996208019554615, -0.012322877533733845, -0.01639946922659874, 0.011445047333836555, 0.006404172163456678, -0.0014904829440638423, 0.013712775893509388, -0.005549617577344179, -0.0039568874053657055, 0.042534876614809036, 0.009170668199658394, 0.03737429901957512, -0.022823592647910118, -0.0012926385970786214, 0.00396021269261837, -0.0008204722544178367, 0.01722409762442112, -0.027265947312116623, 0.02565659023821354, 0.013805879279971123, -0.026880232617259026, 0.005380036775022745, -0.02098812907934189, -0.009064264595508575, 0.00819973461329937, -0.016625577583909035, -0.0035079969093203545, -0.039156559854745865, -0.00025520261260680854, -0.011312042362987995, -0.015641342848539352, 0.014723611064255238, -0.00026351539418